= Digital signature — Technical =

A signature scheme contains KeyGen, Sign, and Verify. Correctness requires Verify(pk,m,Sign(sk,m))=accept. Security is normally defined against existential forgery under chosen-message attack or another explicit model; identity and authorization bindings sit outside the bare cryptographic primitive.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* digital signature ≠ scanned/typed signature
* valid signature ≠ proof of human identity or intent
* signature verification ≠ confidentiality

